{
 "fps": 30,
 "frames": 3149,
 "lines": [
  {
   "n": 1,
   "start": 2,
   "end": 126,
   "text": "In this world, every sorry you owe becomes a balloon tied to your wrist."
  },
  {
   "n": 2,
   "start": 139,
   "end": 193,
   "text": "Say sorry, and it pops."
  },
  {
   "n": 3,
   "start": 206,
   "end": 384,
   "text": "Most people carry two or three. Grandpa Joe carries eleven, so he ties himself to the mailbox at night."
  },
  {
   "n": 4,
   "start": 400,
   "end": 454,
   "text": "The principal wears ankle weights."
  },
  {
   "n": 5,
   "start": 465,
   "end": 554,
   "text": "On picture day, the photographer stands on a ladder."
  },
  {
   "n": 6,
   "start": 566,
   "end": 695,
   "text": "And if you ever float? Everyone knows what that means. You're a bad person."
  },
  {
   "n": 7,
   "start": 708,
   "end": 901,
   "text": "Maya has had one balloon since she was six. Gray. It never pops. No matter who she says sorry to."
  },
  {
   "n": 8,
   "start": 915,
   "end": 1026,
   "text": "Then there's Ezra. Forty-two balloons. He floats to school."
  },
  {
   "n": 9,
   "start": 1038,
   "end": 1161,
   "text": "Kids throw paper at him from the second floor. The teacher ties him to the radiator."
  },
  {
   "n": 10,
   "start": 1175,
   "end": 1265,
   "text": "Even Maya called him a bully. She'd never even talked to him."
  },
  {
   "n": 11,
   "start": 1283,
   "end": 1433,
   "text": "Then, on the field trip to the cliffs, the wind picked up... and Ezra's rope snapped."
  },
  {
   "n": 12,
   "start": 1457,
   "end": 1529,
   "text": "He shot straight up, over the edge, toward the ocean."
  },
  {
   "n": 13,
   "start": 1541,
   "end": 1633,
   "text": "Everyone screamed, \"Say sorry, Ezra! Pop them!\""
  },
  {
   "n": 14,
   "start": 1648,
   "end": 1726,
   "text": "\"I've tried! Every single day! They don't pop!\""
  },
  {
   "n": 15,
   "start": 1748,
   "end": 1927,
   "text": "That's when Maya looked up at her gray balloon. Six years. Never popped."
  },
  {
   "n": 16,
   "start": 1956,
   "end": 2015,
   "text": "Because her dad never said sorry for leaving."
  },
  {
   "n": 17,
   "start": 2039,
   "end": 2167,
   "text": "The balloons were never the sorrys you owe. They're the sorrys people owe you."
  },
  {
   "n": 18,
   "start": 2193,
   "end": 2381,
   "text": "Maya turned to the class. \"We did this. Every name we called him. Every paper we threw.\""
  },
  {
   "n": 19,
   "start": 2401,
   "end": 2512,
   "text": "Silence. Then Jake whispered, \"Sorry, Ezra.\" Pop."
  },
  {
   "n": 20,
   "start": 2528,
   "end": 2659,
   "text": "\"Sorry.\" Pop. \"I'm sorry, Ezra.\" Pop. Pop. Pop."
  },
  {
   "n": 21,
   "start": 2676,
   "end": 2788,
   "text": "Forty-two sorrys later, Ezra floated down, right into their arms."
  },
  {
   "n": 22,
   "start": 2798,
   "end": 3003,
   "text": "Now Ezra walks to school. And Maya's gray balloon? She still has it. But she doesn't hold it alone anymore."
  },
  {
   "n": 23,
   "start": 3019,
   "end": 3124,
   "text": "Like and subscribe... or that's one more balloon for me."
  }
 ],
